   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 185 of the laws of 2005, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the county of Wyoming to impose a county recording tax on\nobligations secured by a mortgage on real property, in relation to the\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7624",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7624-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 185 of 2005",
    "lawSection": "Wyoming County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7624\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 185 of the laws of 2005,\namending the tax law relating to authorizing the county of Wyoming to\nimpose a county recording tax on obligations secured by a mortgage on\nreal property, in relation to the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill extends the expiration date authorizing the county of Wyoming\nto impose a county recording tax on obligations secured by a mortgage on\nreal property.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: states that the act that authorizes the county of Wyoming to\nimpose a county recording tax on obligations secured by a mortgage on\nreal property shall expire December 1, 2021.\n\nSection 2: states that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nArticle IX of the New York State Constitution requires local governments\nto receive state authorization to maintain the levy, collection, and\nadministration of certain local taxes. The Wyoming County Board of\nSupervisors recently requested the state legislature to extend their\nauthority to impose a county recording tax. This bill provides that\nextension.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.6549/A.9419, Chapter 182 of the laws of 2016 FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nOne-quarter of one percent (0.25%) county line recording tax on mort-\ngages on real property in Wyoming County.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
